      "content": "For real-time visibility, use a data logger equipped with a reliable temperature data recording solution that can continuously monitor and securely transmit temperature data. It should have features such as GPS tracking and be able to store a long duration of temperature readings to ensure compliance. Some high-quality data loggers can send live updates with alerts via a mobile app or web portal. Additionally, you may also want to include redundant sensors to verify accuracy. Ensure the chosen system is connected to a central management system for monitoring all the cold chain shipments in real time. Make sure to test and validate the system thoroughly to confirm it performs as expected before deployment. Lastly, consider having contingency plans such as geo-fencing alerts if the shipment leaves the preset parameters, and local backup systems if communication fails in transit.",
